findings.recommendation:
Remove the server-level Content-Type add_header. Instead, add it only inside the `if ($auth_required = 1)` block — but nginx's return directive in an if block doesn't need add_header because `return` generates a synthetic response with no inherited headers. The correct fix is to add `add_header Content-Type 'application/json';` ONLY in the error return:
```nginx
if ($auth_required = 1) {
    add_header Content-Type 'application/json' always;
    return 401 '{"error":"unauthorized",...}';
}
```
Note: nginx `if` in server context allows add_header before return. Alternatively, keep the body as-is — most HTTP clients will interpret the 401 JSON correctly regardless of Content-Type when the body is clearly JSON.
